.TH NEOWALL 1 "2026-10-28" "neowall @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neowall \- GPU shader, image and terminal wallpapers for Wayland and X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neowall
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-date
.IR offset ]
.RB [ \-\-timelapse
.IR span / duration ]
.br
.B neowall
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neowall
draws a wallpaper on every monitor: a still image, a slideshow, a live
GLSL shader (Shadertoy code works unchanged), or a terminal running any
program.
Shaders can react to audio, the time of day, system load and where your
windows are.
.PP
Run without a command,
.B neowall
starts the daemon.
If a daemon is already running, a command talks to it over a socket in
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.PP
On Wayland it needs a compositor with
.B wlr\-layer\-shell
(Hyprland, Sway, river, Wayfire, niri and others) or KDE Plasma.
GNOME on Wayland has no way for a client to draw behind windows, so
.B neowall
refuses to start there; GNOME on X11 works.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Use this config file instead of the default search path (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Stay in the foreground instead of forking.
Implied when started by systemd.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging, including OpenGL driver messages.
.TP
.BI \-\-date " offset"
Shift the clock shaders see, e.g.
.BR +6d ", " \-2h ", " 90m .
Handy for previewing time\-of\-day wallpapers.
.TP
.BI \-\-timelapse " span/duration"
Compress shader time, e.g.
.B 30d/20s
plays thirty days in twenty seconds.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Running daemon
.TP
.B next
Skip to the next wallpaper in a cycle.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume
Pause or resume wallpaper cycling.
.TP
.BR pause\-shader ", " resume\-shader
Freeze or resume shader animation.
.TP
.B reload
Re\-read the config.
If the new file is invalid the old config stays in effect.
.TP
.BI set " index"
Show wallpaper
.I index
(0\-based) of the cycle.
.TP
.B list
List the wallpapers in the cycle with their indices.
.TP
.BR current ", " status
Show what each output is displaying.
.TP
.BI set\-terminal " command"
Replace the program running in a terminal wallpaper.
.TP
.B kill
Stop the daemon.
.TP
.B ping
Exit 0 if a daemon is running and answering, 1 otherwise.
Useful in scripts.
.SS Shader authoring
.TP
.BI new " name"
Write a new shader that runs as is.
.B \-\-template=scene|flat|reactive
picks a starting point;
.B \-\-list
shows them.
.TP
.BI import " export.json" " \fR[\fPname\fR]\fP"
Turn a Shadertoy JSON export into a shader in
.IR ~/.config/neowall/shaders ,
with every pass and its channel bindings.
What can't come over (Shadertoy's own textures and cube maps, music, the
sound pass) is listed and replaced with a built-in.
.B \-\-force
overwrites.
.TP
.BI preview " shader"
Run one shader in the foreground next to the daemon, without touching
your config.
.TP
.BI watch " shader"
Like
.BR preview ,
but recompile on every save and print errors inline.
A broken save keeps the last good shader on screen.
.TP
.BR docs " [\fIword\fR]"
List the helpers and uniforms shaders can use, optionally filtered.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/neowall/config.vibe
User config (falls back to
.IR ~/.config/neowall/config.vibe ).
Created from the installed sample on first run.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/neowall/config.vibe
System\-wide config, used when the user has none.
.TP
.I ~/.config/neowall/shaders/
Your shaders.
Looked up first by bare name.
.TP
.I @DATADIR@/shaders/
Shaders that ship with neowall.
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME
and
.B $XDG_DATA_DIRS
are searched too.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/neowall.sock
Control socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NEOWALL_GL_DEBUG=1
Log OpenGL driver debug messages without full verbose logging.
.TP
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
Pick the display server, as usual.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean exit.
.TP
.B 1
Startup or command failure.
.TP
.B 75
The GPU reset or a surface was lost.
Under systemd the unit restarts
.BR neowall ;
otherwise it restarts itself, at most three times a minute.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start it with your session (systemd):
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now neowall
.fi
.RE
.PP
A shader on one monitor and a slideshow on the other:
.PP
.RS
.nf
output {
  DP\-1     { shader moon_ocean.glsl }
  HDMI\-A\-1 { path ~/Pictures/ duration 600 }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write a shader and watch it as you edit:
.PP
.RS
.nf
neowall new sky \-\-template=scene
neowall watch sky
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neowall.vibe (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/1ay1/neowall
